  "gaps": [
    "Cursor linux-arm64 and WorkBuddy darwin-x64 are outside the pull request matrix and are not pinned here.",
    "npm entries pin each client package's own tarball (integrity and shasum); its dependencies and platform packages still resolve at install time.",
    "Cursor publishes no desktop checksum: the darwin-arm64 and win32-x64-user SHA-256 values and sizes are CI observations from the recorded runs (identical in every recorded run).",
    "The WorkBuddy runtime has no separate artifact or hash: it ships inside the desktop package, and CI checks only its version.",
    "Whether the WorkBuddy win32-x64-user 5.8.3.41334564 reference hash came from the official update feed or the winget manifest was not recorded.",
    "The first records come only from pull request runs of 2026-10-27 and 2026-10-28; the first compatibility monitor run recorded, 41297371104/1 of 2026-11-01, is cited only by the codex, opencode, claude, and codebuddy accepted versions.",
    "The original acceptance of each baseline predates these records and is not part of them.",
    "The WorkBuddy linux-x64-deb baseline reference hash has not matched the download in any recorded run; it stays advisory, and making it strict is a baseline change."
  ]
